#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:37
msgid "Installing a pinned Nix version from a URL"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:39
msgid ""
"Version-specific installation URLs for all Nix versions since 1.11.16 can be "
"found at [releases.nixos.org](https://releases.nixos.org/?prefix=nix/). The "
"directory for each version contains the corresponding SHA-256 hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:42
msgid "All installation scripts are invoked the same way:"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:44
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ export VERSION=2.19.2 \n"
"$ curl -L https://releases.nixos.org/nix/nix-$VERSION/install | sh\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:49
msgid "Multi User Installation"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:51
msgid ""
"The multi-user Nix installation creates system users and a system service "
"for the Nix daemon."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:53
msgid "Supported systems:"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:55
msgid "Linux running systemd, with SELinux disabled"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:58
msgid ""
"To explicitly instruct the installer to perform a multi-user installation on "
"your system:"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:60
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ bash <(curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install) --daemon\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:64
msgid ""
"You can run this under your usual user account or `root`. The script will "
"invoke `sudo` as needed."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:67
msgid "Single User Installation"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:69
msgid "To explicitly select a single-user installation on your system:"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:71
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ bash <(curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install) --no-daemon\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:75
msgid ""
"In a single-user installation, `/nix` is owned by the invoking user. The "
"script will invoke `sudo` to create `/nix` if it doesn’t already exist. If "
"you don’t have `sudo`, manually create `/nix` as `root`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:85
msgid "Installing from a binary tarball"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:87
msgid ""
"You can also download a binary tarball that contains Nix and all its "
"dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:88
msgid ""
"Choose a [version](https://releases.nixos.org/?prefix=nix/) and [system type]"
"(../development/building.md#platforms)"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:89
msgid "Download and unpack the tarball"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:90
msgid "Run the installer"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:92
msgid "**Example**"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:94
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ pushd $(mktemp -d)\n"
"$ export VERSION=2.19.2\n"
"$ export SYSTEM=x86_64-linux\n"
"$ curl -LO https://releases.nixos.org/nix/nix-$VERSION/nix-$VERSION-$SYSTEM."
"tar.xz\n"
"$ tar xfj nix-$VERSION-$SYSTEM.tar.xz\n"
"$ cd nix-$VERSION-$SYSTEM\n"
"$ ./install\n"
"$ popd\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:105
msgid ""
"The installer can be customised with the environment variables declared in "
"the file named `install-multi-user`."
msgstr ""

