#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:119
msgid ""
"This section previously detailed the situation, options, and trade-offs, but "
"it now only outlines what the installer does. You don't need to know this to "
"run the installer, but it may help if you run into trouble:"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:123
msgid "create a new APFS volume for your Nix store"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:124
msgid ""
"update `/etc/synthetic.conf` to direct macOS to create a \"synthetic\" empty "
"root directory to mount your volume"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:126
msgid "specify mount options for the volume in `/etc/fstab`"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:127
msgid "`rw`: read-write"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:128
msgid ""
"`noauto`: prevent the system from auto-mounting the volume (so the "
"LaunchDaemon mentioned below can control mounting it, and to avoid masking "
"problems with that mounting service)."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:131
msgid ""
"`nobrowse`: prevent the Nix Store volume from showing up on your desktop; "
"also keeps Spotlight from spending resources to index this volume"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:151
msgid "if you have FileVault enabled"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:152
msgid "generate an encryption password"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:153
msgid "put it in your system Keychain"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:154
msgid "use it to encrypt the volume"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/installing-binary.md:155
msgid ""
"create a system LaunchDaemon to mount this volume early enough in the boot "
"process to avoid problems loading or restoring any programs that need access "
"to your Nix store"
msgstr ""
